---
/**
 * About page.
 *
 * This is the site's experience-and-trust page. Google's quality guidance leans
 * heavily on whether a site makes clear who is behind it, and for a local
 * service business the same information is what a customer is looking for
 * anyway: who are you, where are you, and can I come and find you.
 *
 * So it states the company number, the registered address and the connection to
 * the photo studio plainly rather than hiding them in the footer.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { areas } from '../data/areas';

const crumbs = [{ name: 'About' }];
const tier1 = areas.filter((a) => a.tier === 1).map((a) => a.name);
---

<Base
  title="About Us"
  description={`The agency side of ${site.legalName}, a walk-in photo studio at ${site.address.street}, ${site.address.postcode}. Web design, marketing and photography from one local team.`}
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />

  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>A photo studio that learned to build websites</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          {site.name} is the agency side of {site.legalName}, the walk-in photo studio at {site.address.street} in
          Surrey Quays. That is an unusual way round to arrive at web design, and it is the reason we work the way
          we do.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap with-aside">
        <div class="prose">
          <h2>How we got here</h2>
          <p>
            The studio came first. Passport photos, portraits, prints, photo gifts — a shop on Lower Road with a
            counter and a queue. Like most small businesses, it needed a website that could take bookings, and like
            most small businesses, what it got the first time round was slow, hard to change and impossible to find
            in search.
          </p>
          <p>
            So we built it ourselves, then the booking system behind it, then the order and invoicing system that
            still runs the studio today. Other businesses on the street saw it working and asked. That is genuinely
            the whole origin story: we are not a marketing agency that discovered local business, we are a local
            business that had to learn this to survive and then got asked to do it for the neighbours.
          </p>

          <h2>What that means for your project</h2>
          <p>
            We have been the client. We know what it is like to be quoted for a website by someone who will not
            explain what any of it is for, to pay a monthly fee for marketing with no way of telling whether it is
            working, and to be told a rebuild will take six weeks and then wait five months.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>A fixed price before work starts.</strong> A written plan, a timeline and a number. No hourly
              creep.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Plain English.</strong> If we cannot explain why something is worth paying for, you should not
              pay for it.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>An honest no.</strong> We will tell you when ads are the wrong answer, when your existing site
              is worth repairing rather than replacing, and when the free half of local SEO is all you actually need.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>You own everything.</strong> The design, the content, the domain and the accounts. You can
              leave whenever you like and take it all with you.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Local, in the literal sense</h2>
          <p>
            Search for a web designer in Surrey Quays and most of what comes back is agencies in other counties
            running a page for every postcode in Britain. There is nothing illegal about it, but they cannot meet you
            on Tuesday, they have never walked down Lower Road, and they do not know that {tier1.join(', ')} are
            four different markets rather than one.
          </p>
          <p>
            We are at {site.address.street}, {site.address.locality} {site.address.postcode}. You can walk in. We
            work across {areas.length} areas of London and each one has <a href="/areas/">its own page</a>, written
            about that place.
          </p>

          <h2>The legal bit</h2>
          <p>
            {site.name} is a trading name of {site.legalName}, registered in England and Wales, company number {
              site.companyNumber
            }. Registered office: {site.address.street}, {site.address.locality} {site.address.postcode}. You can
            look us up at Companies House — we would rather you did.
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="aside-card">
          <h2>Find us</h2>
          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>Studio</dt>
              <dd>{site.address.street}<br />{site.address.locality} {site.address.postcode}</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Phone</dt>
              <dd><a href={`tel:${site.phone}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a></dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Email</dt>
              <dd><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Instagram</dt>
              <dd>
                <a href={site.instagram} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{site.instagramHandle}</a>
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Company number</dt>
              <dd>{site.companyNumber}</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Start a project</a>
          <p>
            The photo studio at the same address is <a href={site.sister.url} rel="noopener">{site.sister.name}</a>.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-alt">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>What we are not</h2>
          <p>Worth saying, so you can rule us out quickly if we are the wrong fit.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="trust-row">
          <li>
            <strong>Not a template shop</strong>
            <span>Everything is designed for the business. If you want a £200 theme install, we are not it.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Not a big agency</strong>
            <span>You get the people doing the work, not an account manager relaying messages.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Not an SEO guarantee</strong>
            <span>Nobody can promise a Google position. Anyone who does is selling you something else.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Not locked in</strong>
            <span>Projects are fixed price. Marketing is month to month, thirty days notice.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <CtaBand />
  </main>
</Base>
